H2('How much simulation does machine learning save?')
P(f'In the screening scenario, models were trained only on the {ml["n_train_screen"]} diversity-selected frameworks (about 10% of the data) and used to rank the other {ml["n_test_screen"]}. The RF still achieves ρ = {f2(rfs["spearman"])} (MAE = {f3(rfs["MAE"])}), slightly better than RFs trained on ten random subsets of the same size (ρ = {rnd["spearman"]:.2f} ± {rnds["spearman"]:.2f}). The diversity selection therefore helps, but only modestly. The practical question is how many simulations are needed to find the best materials. If the remaining frameworks are simulated in the order predicted by the RF, {eff["RF_screen"]["recall_at_10pct"]*100:.0f}% of the true top-5% are found after simulating 10% of them and {eff["RF_screen"]["recall_at_20pct"]*100:.0f}% after 20%, compared with {eff["random_recall_at_10pct"]*100:.0f}% after 10% for random ordering (Fig. 4c). Recovering 80% of the top performers requires simulating {eff["RF_screen"]["frac_needed_for_80pct"]*100:.0f}% of the candidates. This is a saving of roughly {1/eff["RF_screen"]["frac_needed_for_80pct"]:.0f}-fold relative to exhaustive simulation, at the cost of the {ml["n_train_screen"]} training simulations.')
P(f'Uncertainty estimates are informative but imperfect. The spread of RF tree predictions correlates with the absolute error (ρ = {unc["RF_treestd_vs_abs_err_spearman"]:.2f}), and the 20% of predictions with the largest spread have a mean error of {unc["RF_MAE_highunc20"]:.3f}, compared with {unc["RF_MAE_lowunc80"]:.3f} for the rest.' + (f' For SchNet, neither the ensemble spread (ρ = {unc["SchNet_ens_std_vs_abs_err_spearman"]:.2f}) nor the Monte-Carlo-dropout spread (ρ = {unc["SchNet_mc_std_vs_abs_err_spearman"]:.2f}) carries useful information about the error in this small-data regime.' if 'SchNet_ens_std_vs_abs_err_spearman' in unc else '') + ' Uncertainty can therefore be used to send the least certain candidates to explicit simulation, but it should not be read as a calibrated confidence interval.')
